{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>I crushed them</b>, <b>arise</b> — the verb-form is as when it falls out."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The syntax of Ibn Ezra's Hebrew is elliptical here; rendered hyper-literally. He likely means the form אמחצם parallels the grammatical pattern of קום when used as an imperative or in a comparable construction, but the argument is left compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:43.611948669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}